" Magistrates/Hearing Officers | First Judicial Circuit of Florida Search Public Legal Professionals General Information Judges Public Legal Professionals General Information Judges Search balance Administrative Orders & Directives groups_2 Conflict Counsel important_devices Court Hearings by ZOOM interpreter_mode Court Interpreting hearing Court Mediation edit_document Court Reporting monitor Courtroom Technology man Expert Witness Registry gavel Judges menu_book Law Library reduce_capacity Magistrates/Hearing Officers article Process Servers Home / Legal Professionals / Magistrates/Hearing Officers Magistrates/Hearing Officers In Florida's trial court system, magistrates assist judges by handling specific matters to manage the court’s workload. They conduct hearings, make findings of fact, and provide recommendations on issues such as family law, child support, and custody disputes. Magistrates also draft proposed orders for judges to review. Their recommendations are subject to a judge's approval, ensuring that final judicial authority remains with the judges. Child support hearing officers specialize in child support matters, conducting hearings and making recommendations on child support obligations to expedite resolution within the judicial system. All hearing officers' decisions are subject to judicial review to uphold the integrity of the court's oversight and legal standards. Magistrates escambia county okaloosa county escambia county Charles Britt escambia county Learn More Keith A. McIver escambia county Learn More Sydney L. Taylor Hubley escambia county Learn More okaloosa county Anne M. \"Amy\" McBride okaloosa county Learn More Hearing Officers escambia county okaloosa county escambia county Chris Ferry escambia county Learn More okaloosa county Mark Rubin okaloosa county Learn More About Us The First Judicial Circuit is one of 20 judicial circuits in Florida. Our courts serve the people of Escambia, Okaloosa, Santa Rosa, and Walton Counties. Links Pub